<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-17605] Do not wait forever in upcall cache if entry could not be refreshed</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17605</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The process of refreshing an entry via &lt;tt&gt;refresh_entry()&lt;/tt&gt; goes through an upcall/downcall. If the upcall succeeds, we enter a wait queue. If after that the downcall is never called, we hit the expiry timeout, and we get removed from the wait queue. But if the entry is not new, the expiry time will be &lt;tt&gt;MAX_SCHEDULE_TIMEOUT&lt;/tt&gt;, which is actually an infinite wait because we have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;#define MAX_SCHEDULE_TIMEOUT            LONG_MAX
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So avoid waiting forever if an entry could not be refreshed, and call &lt;tt&gt;wake_up_all()&lt;/tt&gt; if the wait for the ACQUIRING state failed.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
